WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:07.279
For a few years, it seemed like Hayden Christensen
could be Hollywood's next big thing—but

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:12.240
then he pretty much disappeared. Where the
heck did he go, and what caused his exit?

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.110
No help from 'Star Wars'

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.600
Everyone may be all about Star Wars today,
but after the release of the prequel trilogy,

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.619
the franchise was a shadow of its former self.
And Christensen's performance as Anakin Skywalker

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:27.130
was frequently singled out for scorn. New
York Times critic A.O. Scott compared Christensen's

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.980
efforts, along with Natalie Portman's, to
something you might see on an episode of Dawson's

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.930
Creek. The Razzie Awards had a field day with
Christensen. He was awarded Worst Supporting

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:38.800
Actor for both Attack of the Clones and Revenge
of the Sith. By the time the trilogy ended,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.610
it was hard to separate Christensen's performances
from the maligned movies.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.580
No hits

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:48.290
After the dust settled from his time as Anakin,
Christensen starred in one flop after another.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:53.300
Among the very worst: the 2007 thriller Awake,
co-starring Jessica Alba, which grossed just

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:58.270
$14 million in the U.S. and earned a 23 percent
score on Rotten Tomatoes. Christensen followed

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:02.640
Awake with the head-scratching Jumper, which
earned an even lower score of 16 percent despite

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.619
a pretty decent run at the box office. But
then there was Takers, which actually beat

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:11.439
out the Rotten Tomatoes scores of Awake and
Jumper...with a twenty-eight percent.

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:12.920
Ouch.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.450
'Star Wars' ruined his credibility

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:19.060
Ironically, before Attack of the Clones came
out in 2002, Christensen was considered by

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:22.850
many to be one of the fastest-rising young
stars in Hollywood. Much of that had to do

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.749
with his performance in the 2001 Kevin Kline
drama Life as a House, in which he played

00:01:26.749 --> 00:01:30.789
a son whose father tries to reconnect with
him after he learns he's dying of cancer.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:34.069
Christensen was even said to be in contention
for an Oscar nomination. He missed the final

00:01:34.069 --> 00:01:37.659
cut, but with Golden Globe and Screen Actors
Guild nominations instead, one might argue

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:39.289
he was sixth in line that year.

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:42.899
Meanwhile, sandwiched in between Attack of
the Clones and Revenge of the Sith was Shattered

00:01:42.899 --> 00:01:46.759
Glass. In that film, Christensen garnered
praise for his portrayal of journalist Stephen

00:01:46.759 --> 00:01:50.649
Glass, who wrote fabricated stories for The
New Republic in the '90s. The film proved

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:54.689
to be a much-needed reminder of Christensen's
dramatic chops, but it received far less attention

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:58.259
than Revenge of the Sith two years later.
By the time he fully transformed into Darth

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:01.179
Vader, his star seemed to fall right back
to Earth.

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:02.899
Walked away from fame

00:02:02.899 --> 00:02:06.530
Although he faced his fair share of hardships
during and after the release of Attack of

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.819
the Clones and Revenge of the Sith, Christensen
revealed in 2015 that part of his disappearance

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:14.390
from the spotlight was deliberate. According
to an interview with The Los Angeles Times

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:18.390
in December of that year, Christensen bought
a piece of farmland after Star Wars and pretty

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.580
much peaced out:

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.560
"I guess I felt like I had this great thing
in Star Wars that provided all these opportunities

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.330
and gave me a career, but it all kind of felt
a little too handed to me. I didn't want to

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.550
go through life feeling like I was just riding
a wave."

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.830
Christensen wound up spending about five years
away from movie sets. He made headlines in

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:37.610
September 2015 when he returned to the big
screen in the faith-based drama 90 Minutes

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:41.750
in Heaven—which, sadly, was greeted with
scathing reviews, a 24 percent score on Rotten

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.280
Tomatoes, and grossed just $4.8 million at
the box office. Maybe it's time to head back

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.490
to the farm...

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:48.310
Family man

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.210
While he's not the movie star he once was,
Christensen's doing just fine at home with

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.570
his girlfriend of many years, actress Rachel
Bilson, and their daughter, Briar Rose. Christensen

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.480
reportedly met Bilson while working on the
movie Jumper. According to E! Online, the

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.460
couple got engaged in December 2008. It was
called off in August 2010, but they reconciled

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.040
three months later. They welcomed Briar Rose
in October 2014.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.530
He told E! Online in 2015:

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:14.540
"I have this little angel in my life now and
Rachel and I are so thrilled. We don't sleep

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.380
as much as we used to, but it's all so worth
it."

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.320
In 2016, Bilson posted this photo to Instagram
of Christensen blowing bubbles for their daughter,

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.510
revealing their happy home life away from
movie sets. And Bilson has nothing but

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:27.140
lovely things to say about her partner. She
told Health magazine:

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.960
"He's so incredibly supportive and considerate
… I've been in my relationship for seven

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.540
years, so we've grown up together in a way.
This is my partner, my support, just there

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.250
for me no matter what. And vice versa."

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:38.560
With that kind of love, who needs Hollywood?

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.210
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.510
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know why you think Hollywood lost Hayden's

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.010
number...

